a customer has a name and a price.
a product has a name and a price.
to give a customer a discount of some percent:
    reduce the customer's price by the percent percent.
to give a product a discount of some amount:
    reduce the product's price by the amount.
give ann a discount of 10 percent.
to feed customer some food:
    say "yum".
to pay a customer some amount:
    say "paid".
to compare a customer to a customer:
    say "same".
to thank a customer for some reason:
    say "thanks".
thank ann for.
thank ann for "coming" today.
thank ann bob for "coming".
thank every for "coming".
to greet a customer:
    say "hi".
greet every customer and every product.
to introduce a customer to another customer:
    say "hello".
introduce every customer to every customer.
